        "field_id": "question_4468354007",
        "label": "What excites you about this opportunity?",
        "type": "textarea",
        "canonical_field": "essay:generated:question_4468354007",
        "action": "fill",
        "value": "What draws me to Perpay is that the modeling problem is inseparable from the consequence. Decisions about credit for people with subprime scores are exactly the kind of place where a model's failure modes matter more than its headline metric. At Summer Atlantic Capital I build the machine-learning core of an anomaly-detection system, and the thing I spend most of my time on is not raw detection performance but prioritization and explanation: temporal sequence models over event streams feeding a learning-to-rank layer, plus a retrieval-augmented explanation layer so an analyst can see why something was flagged. A system that floods people with alerts creates a second problem instead of solving the first. I did similar translation work on a Gates Foundation health-equity project, training XGBoost models on a national survey dataset of roughly 10 million records and using SHAP to figure out which variables were actually driving predictions, then working with the PI on specification. Perpay has a decade of real repayment behavior across 500,000+ customers and a mission that makes the downside of a bad prediction concrete. That is the kind of data and the kind of stakes I want to work on.",
        "reason": "Essay generated from the operator's about-me context"
